{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "IR4302MTRPBF",
 "kind": "audio",
 "manufacturer": "Infineon",
 "title": "Two-channel Class D audio amplifier with integrated MOSFETs, PQFN44 7 x 7 mm",
 "source": {
  "revision": "Apr 3, 2013",
  "pages": 17
 },
 "summary": "The IR43x2 family (IR4302, IR4322, IR4312) puts a two-channel analog-input PWM controller and four power MOSFETs in one 7 x 7 mm PQFN44. Each channel is a half bridge, and the two can be bridged; supplies may be split or single and inputs single-ended or differential. The controller has its own floating input supply, UVLO on every supply, over-current, over-temperature and self-resetting shutdown, and open-drain CLIP and FAULT outputs. The three parts differ in MOSFET voltage, on-resistance and current rating.",
 "key_figures": [
