 "circuits": [
  {
   "id": "inverting",
   "title": "Inverting amplifier, split supply",
   "page": 3,
   "description": "Two channels on +B and -B rails, each input driving the inverting pin through a series capacitor and resistor, with IN+1 and IN+2 grounded. A resistor from each VS output back to its IN- pin closes the loop; between IN- and COMP a two-capacitor network with a resistor to GND forms the integrator, and a further capacitor takes COMP to GND. An optional external clock reaches both IN- pins through its own capacitor and resistor. VAA and VSS are fed from +B and -B through resistors and bypassed to GND; the CSD capacitor goes to VSS. VCC comes from a separate supply referred to -B through a resistor, and the same supply charges each bootstrap capacitor through a resistor and diode. Each CSH pin connects through a diode to +B. Each VS output drives an LC filter into a speaker returned to GND.",
