   "id": "single-supply",
   "title": "Single power supply (inverting amplifier)",
   "page": 4,
   "description": "One +B rail referred to ground. A resistor divider with an electrolytic capacitor across each half makes a mid-supply node; the GND pin, the compensation returns, the VAA and VSS bypass capacitors, the output filter capacitors and both speakers sit on that node. COM, VN1, VN2, the VCC supply and the VSS feed resistor go to ground. Inputs, feedback, compensation, bootstrap and CSH diodes follow the differential circuit.",
