 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Architecture",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Each channel is an analog error amplifier (an OTA with transconductance near 10 mS) whose output at COMP feeds a PWM comparator switching at (VAA - VSS)/2; the comparator drives a high-side and a low-side MOSFET forming a half bridge from VPn to VNn. The package needs no mechanical heatsink in typical music playback."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Supplies",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "Three supply domains: VCC (10 V to 15 V, referred to COM) for the low-side drivers; VBn, a bootstrap rail held 10 V to 14 V above VSn, for each high-side driver; and the floating input section between VAA and VSS (VAA 4.5 V to 15 V above VSS). VAA-VSS, VCC-COM and VBn-VSn each have an internal shunt zener of about 15 V (VCC, VBS) or about ±5.1 V about GND (VAA, VSS); the clamp current is limited to 20 mA absolute and 1 mA to 15 mA recommended. VN1 and VN2 must be wired to COM."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Under-voltage lockout",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "VCC turns on at 8.9 V typ and off at 8.7 V typ; each VBS at 8.5 V and 8.3 V; the floating input supply VAA-VSS at 8.7 V and 8.2 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Start-up oscillation",
   "page": 9,
   "text": "With CSD at GND the COMP pin oscillates locally at 0.7 MHz to 1.5 MHz."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Shutdown and self reset (CSD)",
   "page": 10,
   "text": "A capacitor on CSD sets the shutdown timing; CSD is charged and discharged at 100 µA typ. The shutdown release threshold Vth1 is 0.70 x VAA typ and the self-reset threshold Vth2 is 0.30 x VAA typ. CSD also serves as a shutdown input. The shutdown propagation delay is 250 ns max."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Over-current protection",
   "page": 10,
   "text": "Each channel trips at +16 A or -16 A typ output current and shuts down within 500 ns max. The high-side sense input CSHn is referred to VSn and is operated between VSn and VBn."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Over-temperature protection",
   "page": 10,
   "text": "The controller shuts down at 105 °C typ junction temperature, with 7 °C hysteresis."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Clip detection",
   "page": 10,
   "text": "CLIP responds when COMP rises above 0.90 x VAA or falls below 0.10 x VAA typ; the detection delay is 40 ns typ and the minimum output duration 3 µs typ. CLIP and FAULT are open-drain outputs referred to GND, each rated for 5 mA sink."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Compensation and switching",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "Each COMP pin needs at least 1 nF of phase compensation to GND. Switching frequency is up to 500 kHz; dead time is 50 ns typ."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heatsink",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "Without a heatsink VPn is limited to 46 V (IR4302, IR4322) or 32 V (IR4312); with one, to 62 V (IR4302), 50 V (IR4322) or 32 V (IR4312)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Board mounting",
   "page": 17,
   "text": "Mounting guidance for the PQFN package is in application note AN-1170."
  }
 ],
